489 - Jesus, Lover of My Soul
 / 
Key: Eb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 489
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[Eb/Bb]Jesus, lover [Bb]of my soul,
[Bb]Let me [Bb7]to thy bosom [Cm/G]fly,
[Gm]While the billows [Bb]near me roll,
[Bb]While [Bb7]the tempest [Gm]still is high;
[Ab]Hide me, [Gm]O my Savior, hide!
[Gm]Till the storm of life is past;
[Bb]Safe into the haven [Eb/Bb]guide,
[Bb]O receive [Bb7]my soul at [Cm/G]last!

Verse 2:
[Eb/Bb]Other refuge [Bb]has I none,
[Bb]Hangs my [Bb7]helpless soul on [Cm/G]thee;
[Gm]Leave O leave me [Bb]not alone!
[Bb]Still [Bb7]support [Cm/G]and [Gm]comfort me;
[Ab]All my [Gm]trust on Thee is stayed,
[Gm]All my help from Thee I bring;
[Bb]Cover my defenseless [Eb/Bb]head
[Bb]With the [Bb7]shadow of Thy [Cm/G]wing.

Verse 3:
[Eb/Bb]Thou, O Christ, all [Bb]I want,
[Bb]More than [Bb7]all in Thee I [Cm/G]find;
[Gm]Raise the fallen, [Bb]cheer the faint,
[Bb]Heal [Bb7]the sick, [Cm/G]and [Gm]lead the blind.
[Ab]Just and [Gm]holy is Thy name,
[Gm]I am all unrighteousness;
[Bb]Vile and full of sin [Eb/Bb]I am;
[Bb]Thou art [Bb7]full of truth and [Cm/G]grace.

Verse 4:
[Eb/Bb]Plenteous grace with [Bb]Thee is found-
[Bb]Grace to [Bb7]pardon all my [Cm/G]sin;
[Gm]Let the healing [Bb]streams abound,
[Bb]Make [Bb7]and keep [Cm/G]me [Gm]pure within;
[Ab]Thou of [Gm]life the Fountain art,
[Gm]Freely let me take of Thee;
[Bb]Spring Thou up within my [Eb/Bb]heart,
[Bb]Rise to [Bb7]all eternity.
